sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, DECISIONS R1-R4 + 1 (certificate signing is the one step call), metrics.exporter_enable decisions (reload, don't restart), single-swamp-node. docs/reference/metrics.md.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: metrics:enable
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane G icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Node 12<br/>Prometheus·Grafana
  participant G as Gateway Node<br/>Caddy for Grafana
  CLI->>GW: metrics:enable 12<br/>Node id or name
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit metrics:enable 12`
  %%> - syntax: `[node] [--json]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the Node that runs Prometheus and Grafana; in a terminal the CLI lists the active Nodes and asks
  %%> - with `--json` or without a terminal, the Node is required (`metrics.node_required`)
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - gives Node 12 the `metrics` role, and shows its dashboards at `https://metrics.orbit`
  Note over GW: Check, claim the role<br/>role: provisioning · task #5173
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - exactly one active Gateway Node, and your Node has an access grant to it
  %%> - Node 12 is an active, managed Linux Node
  %%> - no Node has the `metrics` role yet, not even a failed one (`node.role_conflict`)
  %%> - no other Metrics change runs; the Gateway holds one Metrics lock
  %%> Builds:
  %%> - the Prometheus configuration with every selected exporter Node as a target
  %%> - Grafana's datasource and 3 dashboards, and both container specs with pinned images
  %%> - the Grafana firewall rules, the Caddy site on the Gateway Node, and the private DNS name
  %%> Secrets:
  %%> - creates the Grafana `admin` password once, stored encrypted; a later enable reuses it
  %%> - pushes it to the Swamp vault as key `metrics-role-operation-5173`; the inputs hold only that name
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the `metrics` assignment on Node 12 recorded with status provisioning
  %%> - task #5173 recorded with the full intent
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-metrics-role
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209)
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the configuration files, container specs, exporter list and publication
  %%> - the vault key name of the Grafana password
  %%> - Node 12's and the Gateway Node's addresses and SSH host keys; the SSH identity comes from the `swamp` role
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5173
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
  SW->>N: Install Docker<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/apt · systemd
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - installs `docker.io` when no healthy Docker is present, and keeps it running
  %%> - waits for a busy apt lock within the run's time budget
  SW->>N: Write the configuration<br/>promtool check, then publish
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - writes the Prometheus configuration as a candidate and validates it with `promtool` first
  %%> - publishes it and the Grafana provisioning files in `/etc/orbit/metrics`
  %%> How:
  %%> - official `@swamp/cfgmgmt/directory` and `@swamp/cfgmgmt/file` behaviors over SSH from 209
  SW->>N: Write the Grafana password<br/>vault.get → stdin · mode 0400
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - reads the password from the vault and writes the protected password file through stdin
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the password never appears in inputs, outputs or logs (R3)
  SW->>N: Start the containers<br/>Prometheus · Grafana
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - pulls the pinned images and starts `orbit-metrics-prometheus` and `orbit-metrics-grafana`
  %%> - keeps the named data volumes, so a re-enable continues with the old data
  %%> Gentle:
  %%> - a container whose spec is unchanged keeps running; only a changed configuration is applied, with a Prometheus reload
  %%> - a container is recreated only when its spec or image changes
  %%> How:
  %%> - official `@swamp/cfgmgmt` behaviors (docker_image, systemd, docker_container) over SSH from 209
  SW->>N: Check health once<br/>/-/ready · Grafana /api/user
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - checks Prometheus answers ready, and Grafana accepts the `admin` login
  Note over SW: Add the fleet exporters<br/>same steps as exporter:enable
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - for each selected Node: the exporters, their WireGuard listeners and the firewall allows for Node 12
  %%> - the same steps that `metrics:exporter:enable` runs for one Node
  %%> Which Nodes:
  %%> - every eligible Node with a role that takes part in Metrics, or an `enabled` preference, and Node 12 itself
  SW->>GW: Sign metrics.orbit cert<br/>operation:direct:certificate-sign
  %%> How:
  %%> - a step creates the key on the Gateway Node and reads only the CSR
  %%> - the Gateway signs it with the Orbit CA; this is the one call a step may make to the Gateway
  GW-->>SW: Signed certificate<br/>leaf + chain
  %%> What happens next:
  %%> - Swamp writes the certificate beside its key on the Gateway Node
  SW->>N: Allow the Gateway in<br/>ufw · Grafana port 3000
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - allows only the Gateway Node to reach Grafana on port 3000, and denies other peers
  %%> - places the allow above the deny, and both above broad WireGuard trust
  %%> How:
  %%> - official `@swamp/cfgmgmt/firewall` over SSH from 209
  SW->>G: Publish metrics.orbit<br/>validate, reload Caddy · DNS
  %%> Open:
  %%> - the DNS part is under the DNS hold; Nick decides
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - adds the `metrics.orbit` site to the Gateway Node's Caddyfile, validates it, and reloads Caddy gracefully
  %%> - Caddy asks the Gateway to authorize each request, then proxies over WireGuard to Grafana
  %%> - publishes `metrics.orbit` to the Gateway's WireGuard address through the shared DNS step on the `vpn` Node
  alt every step passes
    G-->>SW: metrics.orbit answers
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - Caddy serves the site with the new certificate
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway for a result
    Note over GW: Record result<br/>role: active · task succeeded
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the `metrics` role on Node 12 becomes active
    %%> - each fleet exporter is recorded as active
    %%> - task #5173 succeeds
  else a step fails
    N--xSW: exit ≠ 0 or not ready
    %%> When:
    %%> - a package, config validation, container, health check, exporter, certificate, firewall or Caddy step fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its error code
    Note over GW: Mark the role failed<br/>keep assignment · resume step
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the assignment and the Grafana password stay; the role is marked failed with the step's error code
    %%> - task #5173 fails
    %%> On the Node:
    %%> - finished steps stay, so a publication failure keeps the running containers; there is no rollback
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - Swamp resumes from the failed step; finished steps don't run again
    %%> - a new enable is refused while the failed assignment exists; converge it with `orbit node:role:add 12 metrics --converge`
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5173
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
